      {
        "id": "source-coordinate-rays-and-vector-marks",
        "description": "FIRST pixels show x/y/z-like terminal letters, three arrow-marked i/j/k-like labels, an internal leftward arrow on the x branch and an upward arrow on the vertical branch. Modernization gives the printed arrowed j label a corresponding short arrow on the y branch, and makes the nearly vertical source fragments exactly collinear. The full x/y rays and upper z segment have no added terminal arrowheads. Projected axes are not asserted perpendicular in the image plane.",
